  "notes": "The research says to treat the self-harmonised vocal stack in 3rds and octaves as a chordal instrument, and that is the one instruction in this batch that maps to a single number: `countermelody.densityRatio` 0.6 with octave_echo weighted 4 to arp’s 2, the densest counter here. Everything else follows from the two populations, which are authored as modes because the research gives them different kits: 130–140 with the clap on 3, and 100–106 with the full ratchet 2&4 kit. Between those, three things are his and not the lane’s: real R&B motion instead of the 2-chord vamp (a ii–V–I borrowing with `borrowed.V` 0.25, seventh 0.5, ninth 0.28); the guitar he actually plays as `timbreHint`; and a bass authored as `offbeat_8ths` at `followRootsProb` 0.65, because the research says the electric bass plays syncopated 8ths against the kick on the R&B-leaning cuts, while the 808 keeps the slow portamento (`portamentoMs` 110, the longest in this batch). The drumless sung tag is `sectionRules.outro` with drums dropped. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The inferred parameter is the hand-percussion: conga and timbale are named as fills, but the [2,5] per-bar density that puts them in the kit is a reading of “layered”, not a sourced count. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.6 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.6 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 46 to 44 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 45 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 2.",
